## ## DEFINITION
iTOL (Interactive Tree Of Life) is an online tool used to visualize, annotate, customize, and share phylogenetic trees.

## PURPOSE
- Visualize phylogenetic trees.
- Annotate tree data.
- Customize tree appearance.
- Share and export publication-quality trees.

## FEATURES
- Interactive tree visualization.
- Color-coding and annotation of branches and labels.
- Supports multiple dataset overlays (heatmaps, bar charts, symbols, etc.).
- Export trees in various image formats.

## FILES TO UPLOAD
- Newick (.nwk, .tree, .tre)
- Nexus (.nex)
- PhyloXML (.xml)
- Annotation files (TXT/CSV format)

## IMPORTANT POINTS
- Web-based and easy to use.
- Supports large phylogenetic trees.
- Produces publication-quality figures.
- Widely used for phylogenetic tree visualization and annotation.
